    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="1375" n="1261" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    J.C.S. Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, Allied Force Headquarters</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Eisenhower</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Combined Chiefs of
                            Staff
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-01">1 September
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    W–8899/9175. Signal from General C<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d599-f1"/> states that reply is in affirmative (To AGWar for Combined Chiefs of Staff and to USFor for British Chiefs of Staff signed
                    Eisenhower cite 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">fhdsc</hi>. This is 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Naf</hi>
                     348) and that he will arrive at the appointed meeting place tomorrow
                    September 2.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
